 "format": "webtracker",
 "version": 1,
 "song": {
  "name": "interstellar",
  "bpm": 120,
  "ticksPerBeat": 4,
  "length": 1440,
  "info": "Interstellar travel: a three minute soundscape, made only from webtracker nodes. 120 bpm, 90 bars.\n\nshep   a Shepard tone: an additive synth with only the octave partials lit rises six octaves in three minutes (an lfo on its pitch input) while two fixed band-pass filters are the window, so it climbs and never gets higher.\npad    the chords of the demo song (Em7, Dmaj7, Cmaj7, Am11, Bm7, Cmaj7, Em9, a second pass that swells higher, a breath on a long Em9, a third pass that builds to the biggest swells, and a long Em9 to end), six voices each, the outer notes quieter so the shape fades at both ends.\nsub    a sine under each chord.\nwind   pink noise through a band-pass an lfo breathes, in a big hall, widened with the spectral panner.\nrise   noise through a high-pass that climbs five octaves while it swells; a Shiva delay takes hold as it climbs (an envelope opens its mix and feedback), so the pattern goes on, wide, when the swell cuts, into a long shimmer tail (23 s, 47 s, 71 s, 103 s, 143 s, 151 s and 167 s).\ntick   a clock every 1.25 s, always the same tick.\nstars  chord tones two octaves up, soft, through two echoes (dotted eighth and a quarter) and a shimmer; denser in the second half."
 },
